armada manifest — one repository's stack: ports, services, checks

VERBS
  config <scan|verify>  report the evidence, then verify what was written
  init                  claim this workspace: ports, .armada/, setup
  up [<component>]      start this workspace's services; wait until they answer
  down [<component>]    stop this workspace's services; keep the port block
  status                what is running, what is mine, what is stale
  check [<selector>]    lint, format and test — the verb a gate calls
  skills [show <name>]  what this repository knows about itself
  components            what this repository can be filtered by
  commands              the verbs this repository declares
  clean                 release what this workspace owns
  <name>                a verb this repo declares; manifest commands lists them

NOT BUILT YET
  render, agents-md, explain  claimed; each answers `not built yet`

`armada manifest <verb> --help` for one verb's usage and flags.

A workspace is one checkout, with services and ports that are only its own.
Claim it and you can run two branches of the same repository at once without
either one taking the other's port or stopping the other's database.
